# @mirror/spectral/score — the orchestra's shared score; the
# eigenboard envelope + metalogue bus + pending kintsugi state, named
# collectively as the score the voices play through.
#
# THE T11 PREREQUISITE the `oscillate.mirror` forward-promise named.
# Lines 219-226 of `oscillate.mirror` (the substrate gap surfaced
# honestly):
#
#   "`active_pass` reads the oscillation's eigenboard context (the
#    candidate morphism_set; the current shard ref) but the substrate's
#    eigenboard context carrier lives at `@mirror/spectral/score`
#    (forward-promised; does not yet exist). For now, the active_pass
#    signature reads `oscillation` (carrying the loop's position) and
#    emits a `morphism`; the eigenboard context is implicit in the
#    oscillation's `ref` field. A future score sub-shard MAY lift this
#    to a typed eigenboard.context carrier."
#
# This shard lands that forward-promise. After it lands, `active_pass`
# (T11) reads a typed score rather than reaching through an opaque
# anchor `ref`; the eigenboard context becomes substrate-fact at the
# composer altitude.
#
# Load-bearing spec: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §4.5 (the score
# sub-shard sketch — "names the eigenboard envelope + metalogue bus +
# pending kintsugi state collectively as the score; read-only to
# voices; mutations are settled through the convergence's daemon");
# §3.2 (the Pack IS the orchestra; the metalogue IS the score);
# §4.2 (the family root's sub-shard list — the line
# `score: the eigenboard + the metalogue + the kintsugi loop's
# pending state`).
#
# === The recognition: the family root already named this ===
#
# `shards/mirror/spectral.mirror` (the family root) already names
# `@mirror/spectral/score` in its sub-shard list (lines 67-71):
#
#   @mirror/spectral/score  eigenboard envelope + metalogue bus +
#                            pending kintsugi state, named
#                            collectively as the score. Read-only
#                            to voices; mutated through the
#                            convergence.
#
# This shard is the substrate-pull realisation of that already-named
# species. Three components, each already a substrate-declared
# carrier in a sibling shard:
#
#   1. `anchor: ref` — the eigenboard envelope's current shard handle.
#      The substrate ref into `@mirror/store`'s content-addressed
#      Merkle-chain history (per `mirror/store.mirror`); the position
#      the oscillation is anchored on; what `dark_pass` advances when
#      a morphism applies under identity preservation.
#
#   2. `session: metalogue_session` — the metalogue bus (already
#      declared in `metalogue.mirror` as `type metalogue_session =
#      { turns: [turn], opacity: transparency(turn) }`). Carries the
#      orchestra's conversation: who's spoken, what's still opaque,
#      where the consent surface is reading next. The score IS the
#      metalogue at the orchestra altitude (per spec §3.2 — "the Pack
#      already IS the orchestra; the metalogue IS the score").
#
#   3. `pending: morphism_set` — the kintsugi loop's pending state
#      (already declared in `consent.mirror` as
#      `type morphism_set = [morphism]`). Carries the morphisms the
#      formatter has proposed but not yet applied (the consent surface
#      is mid-evaluation; or `query_phi` returned partial; or
#      `dark_pass` is waiting on an identity check). Read by
#      `active_pass` to compose the candidate ranking.
#
# This is the family-root-honest reading: the score is the
# *shared-score-as-orchestra-state*, NOT a per-pulse computation
# artifact. Three substrate-declared carriers, composed into one
# typed record at the orchestra altitude.
#
# === Substrate-pull recognition: the brief proposed a different shape ===
#
# The 22nd-instance candidate (per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]):
# the task brief proposed
#
#   type score = {
#     anchor:     ref
#     candidates: morphism_set
#     operator:   operator       (from sheaf_laplacian.mirror)
#     curvatures: [curvature]    (from curvature.mirror)
#   }
#
# — which would couple the score type to the @epistemologic/math
# numerical primitives. The substrate-pull check surfaced the
# correction:
#
#   - `candidates` ≡ `pending: morphism_set` — same carrier; renamed
#     to honour the family-root's "pending kintsugi state" framing.
#   - `operator` and `curvatures` are NOT score fields; they are the
#     *internal working state of `active_pass`*. The composer altitude
#     computes them on read from `pending`; the score carries the
#     pre-numerical state the voices share, not the derived numerics
#     the formatter recomputes per pulse.
#
# The corrected chain for T11's `active_pass(o: oscillation) -> morphism`:
#
#   1. `score_of(o)` reads the oscillation → typed score (this shard).
#   2. `pending(score)` reads the score → morphism_set (this shard).
#   3. The morphism_set's content refs → gaps via `gaps_of` (T5,
#      Rust today; substrate carrier in `@epistemologic/property`).
#   4. The gaps → tensor via `tensor_of` (T6).
#   5. The tensor → operator via `sheaf_laplacian` (T8).
#   6. The operator's edges → curvatures via `balanced_forman` (T9).
#   7. The curvatures → ranked fractures via `minimize` (T7+T9).
#   8. The top-ranked fracture → morphism (the active_pass return).
#
# `operator` and `curvatures` appear at step 5-6 as *intermediate
# results* of the active_pass body, not as score fields. The score
# stays minimal; the numerics live where they live (under
# @epistemologic/math); the composer composes.
#
# This honours [[feedback-substrate-pull]]: when the substrate already
# names a carrier (morphism_set in consent.mirror; metalogue_session
# in metalogue.mirror; ref in glass.mirror), don't reinvent; use the
# existing primitives. The 22nd instance of substrate-already-had-
# the-word: `score` is what the family-root said it is, not a richer
# numerical envelope.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `glass.mirror`, `ref` is the substrate's reference floor;
# the score's `anchor` rides it directly. Per `metalogue.mirror`,
# `metalogue_session` IS the typed conversation carrier; the score's
# `session` field rides it directly. Per `consent.mirror`,
# `morphism_set = [morphism]` is the typed candidate-list at the
# consent altitude; the score's `pending` rides it directly. Per
# `oscillate.mirror`, `oscillation` carries the loop's live position
# (state + iteration + anchor); the score is derived from an
# oscillation by projecting its anchor + composing with the session
# and pending sets.
#
# This shard declares `score` as a record per the consent.morphism /
# oscillate.oscillation precedent (three named fields, each a typed
# carrier from a sibling shard); `score_of` as the projection action
# from oscillation; `pending` as the read action voices use to see
# the morphism_set the consent surface is evaluating. NO new verdict
# carrier; NO opaque-`ref` carriers where structured types are
# available (per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]).
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
# Each gap below is a forward-promise to a later substrate-pull tick;
# none invented here:
#
#   - `score_of(o)` reads an oscillation and emits a score, but the
#     substrate has no "read the active metalogue session from a
#     shard ref" action declared at the orchestra altitude — the
#     realisation layer reads the session from the running glue-bus
#     state (per CLAUDE.md's "glue bus" discipline) and projects
#     into a metalogue_session carrier. A future
#     `@mirror/spectral/voice` sub-shard MAY declare the
#     session-from-ref projection; for this tick the substrate names
#     the score's shape; the projection arithmetic stays at the
#     realisation layer.
#
#   - `score_of` similarly reads the oscillation's pending morphism
#     set — but the substrate has no "read the kintsugi loop's
#     in-flight morphisms from an anchor ref" action declared at
#     the consumer altitude. The realisation layer reads the
#     `oscillation`'s implicit pending set (carried in the loop's
#     per-tick state) and projects into a morphism_set carrier. A
#     future `@mirror/spectral/audition` sub-shard MAY declare the
#     pending-from-anchor projection (the audition is the natural
#     consumer that materialises pending morphisms into the tournament
#     for resolution). For this tick the substrate names the carrier;
#     the projection arithmetic stays at the realisation layer.
#
#   - `pending(s)` is a pure projection (record field read); no
#     obligation block needed at the substrate altitude beyond the
#     standard `\` discipline. The substrate names the surface; the
#     realisation layer returns `s.pending`.
#
#   - The score is READ-ONLY to voices (per the family-root spec —
#     "mutated through the convergence"). This shard does NOT declare
#     a `mutate(s: score, ...)` action; mutations land through the
#     kintsugi loop (`dark_pass` advances the anchor; the metalogue
#     bus accumulates turns; the consent surface drains pending).
#     The substrate's read-only contract is structural: only
#     `score_of` constructs scores; the constructor is the only
#     mutation path.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Every type and action below names an established object older than
# the discipline of computer science (modulo the discipline names):
#
#   score           Guido d'Arezzo (c.1025), Micrologus; the staff-
#                    notation graph that ensemble voices read in
#                    common. The substrate's reading is the orchestra-
#                    altitude shared state per spec §3.2.
#   anchor          Eilenberg (1942); the categorical fixed-point
#                    object that morphisms hinge on. The substrate's
#                    reading is the eigenboard's current section IS
#                    the morphism-application anchor.
#   session         Marshall McLuhan (1964) Understanding Media;
#                    the bounded conversational unit. The substrate's
#                    reading is metalogue_session per
#                    metalogue.mirror's Bateson 1972 grounding.
#   pending         Carnielli (2002) on the LFI hierarchy; the
#                    formula that holds in the meta-theory but
#                    not yet in the object theory. The substrate's
#                    reading is morphism_set in the consent-pause
#                    state per consent.mirror's pause_event.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* these so the formatter and
# voices read them through one named carrier. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §3.2 (the Pack IS the
#               orchestra; the metalogue IS the score),
#               §4.2 (the family root's sub-shard list — score named
#               as "eigenboard envelope + metalogue bus + pending
#               kintsugi state"),
#               §4.5 (the score sub-shard sketch — read-only to
#               voices; mutated through the convergence),
#               §4.6 (the @mirror/store integration — eigenboard's
#               Merkle-chain history IS the score's recording
#               medium),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-07-prophecy-derived-fractures-
#               from-topology.md (the Crystal sharpens section: the
#               score is pre-crystal; crystal is post-settle; the
#               prophecy is the calendar attached).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the score IS
#                      the lattice element each pulse joins onto;
#                      reads compose monotonically with the bus +
#                      pending; mutations land through the kintsugi
#                      loop's ascent),
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (the
#                      score IS the (A, H, D) triple's H component
#                      observed at the orchestra altitude — the
#                      Hilbert-space-of-states the voices share; the
#                      kintsugi loop's U(t) reads and advances it),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (score_of lifts oscillation → score;
#                      pending projects score → morphism_set; both
#                      lifts substrate-declared in this shard with
#                      sibling-shard primitives),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (score is its own
#                      typed carrier; pending returns morphism_set
#                      not bare list; no opaque ref escapes the
#                      score surface),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (the score's three
#                      fields are all sibling-shard primitives; the
#                      substrate-pull discipline refused the brief's
#                      richer numerical shape in favour of the
#                      family-root's existing definition),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the 22nd-instance recognition: the family
#                      root already named score's role; this shard
#                      realises that already-named species).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `active_pass` (T11) reads
#                  `score_of(oscillation) -> pending -> morphism_set`
#                  as the eigenboard context. The future
#                  `@mirror/spectral/audition` consumer reads the
#                  same pending set as the tournament's input.
#                  Both consumer-pulls are downstream; this shard
#                  declares the carrier and the two read surfaces.
#                  This shard does NOT pull `@mirror/spectral/voice`
#                  or `@mirror/spectral/audition`; the substrate-
#                  altitude arrow points inward (score IS consumed
#                  by active_pass and by audition; not the other
#                  way around).
# Related shards: mirror/spectral.mirror (the family root; declares
#                 this sub-shard as the orchestra's shared-state
#                 species),
#                 mirror/spectral/oscillate.mirror (the loop primitive
#                 whose forward-promise this shard lands; score_of
#                 lifts oscillation → score; T11 active_pass consumes
#                 the lift),
#                 mirror/spectral/consent.mirror (the consent surface;
#                 morphism_set carrier; the pending field rides the
#                 declared type directly),
#                 metalogue.mirror (the metalogue bus; metalogue_session
#                 carrier; the session field rides the declared type
#                 directly),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the eigenboard's Merkle-chain
#                 history; the anchor ref reads into the store's
#                 content-addressed substrate),
#                 epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.mirror (the
#                 numerical sibling that active_pass composes on read
#                 of pending — NOT a score field, but the realisation
#                 layer's working set),
#                 epistemologic/math/curvature.mirror (same — the
#                 SDRF ranking is computed from pending in
#                 active_pass's body, not stored on the score).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/spectral/score.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/spectral/score` as a species under the `@mirror/spectral`
# family.

# === The score carrier ===
#
# The orchestra's shared score. Three components, each a typed
# carrier from a sibling shard:
#
# anchor   — the eigenboard envelope's current shard handle (a ref
#             into `@mirror/store`'s content-addressed Merkle chain).
#             The position the oscillation is anchored on; what
#             `dark_pass` advances when a morphism applies under
#             identity preservation; what voices read to see "where
#             the substrate is now."
# session  — the metalogue bus (per `metalogue.mirror`'s
#             `metalogue_session` carrier). The orchestra's
#             conversation: who's spoken, what's still opaque, the
#             ordered turns that frame the consent surface's reads.
#             The score IS the metalogue at the orchestra altitude
#             (per spec §3.2).
# pending  — the kintsugi loop's pending morphism set (per
#             `consent.mirror`'s `morphism_set` carrier). The
#             morphisms the formatter has proposed but the consent
#             surface has not yet resolved (mid-evaluation; or
#             `query_phi` returned partial; or `dark_pass` is waiting
#             on an identity check). Read by `active_pass` (T11) as
#             the candidate set the SDRF ranking ranks; read by
#             `audition` (forward-promised) as the tournament input.
#
# Identity contract: two scores are equal iff their anchor, session,
# and pending fields all match. The realisation layer enforces.
#
# Read-only contract: voices read the score; the score is not mutated
# directly. Mutations land through the kintsugi loop — `dark_pass`
# advances the anchor when identity preserves; the metalogue bus
# accumulates turns through `@metalogue`'s emit discipline; the
# consent surface drains pending through `query_phi`'s verdict.
# This shard declares only the read surface; mutations are the
# downstream consumers' responsibility.
type score = {
  anchor:  ref,
  session: metalogue_session,
  pending: morphism_set,
}

# === score_of — the projection from oscillation ===
#
# Reads an oscillation (the kintsugi loop's live position) and emits
# the score the formatter and voices read to see the orchestra's
# shared state. The substrate-altitude lift from
# `@kintsugi/oscillate.oscillation` to
# `@mirror/spectral/score.score`.
#
# Composes through:
#
#   1. `oscillation.anchor` → `score.anchor` — direct projection.
#      The oscillation's anchor IS the score's anchor; no
#      computation; the read is a record-field forward.
#   2. The realisation layer reads the running metalogue bus state
#      for the substrate-active session (per CLAUDE.md's glue-bus
#      discipline) and projects into a `metalogue_session` carrier.
#      The substrate names the obligation; the realisation layer
#      discharges via the glue-bus surface (forward-promise to
#      `@mirror/spectral/voice` which MAY substrate-declare the
#      session-from-ref projection).
#   3. The realisation layer reads the oscillation's implicit pending
#      morphism set (carried in the loop's per-tick state) and
#      projects into a `morphism_set` carrier. The substrate names
#      the obligation; the realisation layer discharges via the
#      kintsugi loop's pending-state surface (forward-promise to
#      `@mirror/spectral/audition` which MAY substrate-declare the
#      pending-from-anchor projection).
#
# Per `oscillate.mirror`'s forward-promise (lines 222-226): this
# lift IS what makes `active_pass`'s eigenboard-context-carrier
# substrate-fact rather than implicit-through-the-anchor-ref. After
# this action lands, T11's `active_pass(o: oscillation) -> morphism`
# composes as:
#
#   active_pass(o) =
#     let s        = score_of(o)         -- this action
#     let m_set    = pending(s)          -- this shard's read action
#     let tension_set = tensor_of(gaps_of(m_set.content_refs))
#     let op       = sheaf_laplacian(tension_set.restrictions)
#     let cs       = [ balanced_forman(op, e) | e in op.entries ]
#     let ranked   = minimize(tension_set)   -- SDRF on cs
#     project ranked.head into morphism { content, score, expected }
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# the oscillation's anchor (direct projection), the active metalogue
# session (via the glue bus), and the loop's pending morphisms (via
# the kintsugi loop's per-tick state), emits the three-field score
# record.
score_of(o: oscillation) -> score { \ }

# === pending — the read action voices use ===
#
# Reads a score and emits the pending morphism set (per
# `consent.mirror`'s `morphism_set` carrier). The substrate's
# orchestra-altitude read surface for "what morphisms is the
# formatter mid-evaluation on?"
#
# Composes through:
#
#   1. Direct field projection: `score.pending` → `morphism_set`.
#      No computation; the read IS the record-field forward.
#
# Consumers:
#
#   - `active_pass` (T11) reads `pending(score_of(o))` to compose
#     the candidate set the SDRF ranking ranks. The eigenboard
#     context is now substrate-declared: read pending; compose with
#     gaps_of / tensor_of / sheaf_laplacian / balanced_forman /
#     minimize; project the top fracture into the proposed morphism.
#   - `@mirror/spectral/audition` (forward-promised) reads pending
#     as the tournament's input set; the audition resolves which
#     pending morphism wins the next consent surface.
#   - `@mirror/spectral/voice` (forward-promised) reads pending as
#     the section's open obligations; voices proposing morphisms
#     add to pending; voices resolving morphisms drain pending.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# `s.pending` and emits. The substrate names the surface; the
# arithmetic IS the field read.
pending(s: score) -> morphism_set { \ }

out @mirror/spectral/score
out score
out score_of
out pending
